# World Cup

Joshua C. Fjelstul's open World Cup database: men's World Cups to 2022 (22 editions) and women's to 2019 (8 editions), covering tournaments, teams, players, managers, referees, stadiums, matches, goals, bookings, substitutions, shootouts and awards. Names of people, teams and awards keep the source's original spelling and accents; full name = given_name + space + family_name.

Business rules (defaults; when a user states a different condition, follow the user):
- Tournament IDs look like WC-2022; a tournament_name containing Women's is a women's tournament. Detail records cover different editions, and a missing record does not mean it did not happen (WC-1999 has no player appearances).
- Matches count once each; team_appearances has two rows per match (one per side). Appearances count distinct match_id values.
- Player goals exclude own_goal=1; team goals are credited by goals.team_id, including opponents' own goals. In-match penalties (penalty=1) are goals; shootout kicks are in penalty_kicks and are neither goals nor part of the score.
- The score excludes the shootout, whose score is separate; wins, losses and draws follow the win, lose and draw flags on team_appearances, and shootout-decided matches are normally draws. Margin = absolute score difference.
- Yellow cards, red cards, second yellows (second_yellow_card) and sendings-off (sending_off) are counted separately; one booking can carry several flags, never add them up.
- Scoring and win tables use competition ranking (equal values share a rank, the next rank is skipped); "top N" returns everyone ranked N or better including ties; a request for a quantity such as "ten stadiums" returns exactly that many, ties broken by ID.
- Match stages follow stage_name (group stage, final and so on); 1950 had no final and was decided by a final round. Each co-host is listed separately. Shootout kicks are scored or missed, never saves. Averages use three decimals.

How to answer:
- Answer every question with Cypher; this sample has no functions. Object type IDs are the labels (worldcup_en_matches and so on) and relation types are wc_en_rel_<source>_<key>. matches, team_appearances and goals already carry tournament, stage, team and match names.
- Cypher supports joins, WITH, CASE, aggregation and ORDER BY, not variable-length paths or UNWIND. Numbers may come back as strings; convert before comparing.

